Type: Package
Package: mic.sim
Title: Simulating and Fitting Models to MIC Data
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Alec", "Michael", , "alec.j.michael@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Analyze minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) data: import
    or simulate data, view the distribution, fit models, and visualize the
    fits. Models are latent Gaussian mixtures for interval-censored log2
    MIC values, in which the mixture weights and component means vary
    smoothly over time, to distinguish and track the wild-type and
    non-wild-type subpopulations.
